Decided to transition my build log into .txt files to better comprehend the process going on than the simple git messages and paperback documentation I've been using.
Much has been lost but hopefully this document can be better used to keep track of progress on this project.


The story so far:
I'm using a Hosyond ESP32 N16R8 model with an Elecrow 480 x 320 LCD screen module and a Sparkfun rotary encoder to create a sort of Spotify playback device.

The ESP is connected to my laptop through a USB type c cable in the COM port.

The screen connects to certain GPIO pins with jumper cables.  This is better documented in the GPIO tester file.  Notably, I did not pay for touchscreen capabilities, 
    as this project was designed around using the rotary encoder instead.

The encoder connects to certain GPIO pins with wire.  Passive components and basic filtering are put on the encoder pins to reduce noise to the ESP.  The push button and 
    RGB pins connect through wire as well.


Completed as of 9.17.26 16:00:
Everything is fully wired, as per the electrical diagram in the Documentation folder.  
A basic case CAD file was designed in OnShape, and a copy exists in the hardware folder of this repository.
A basic UI has been designed, as per the UI diagram in the Documentation folder.
A basic README has been written, and is likely to be edited for better clarity at the end of the project.
The rotary encoder works and the ESP fully tracks all input - rotational and button press. The RGB also works, denoting either the direction of rotation or button input.


